statement.paragraph:
Let $H$ be the set of all vectors of the form $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      s \\
      {3s} \\
      {2s}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,.$ Find a vector $\textbf{v}$ in $\text{ℝ}^{3}$ such that $H = \text{span}\left\{ \textbf{v} \right\}$. Why does this show that $H$ is a subspace of $\text{ℝ}^{3}$?

Let $H$ be the set of all vectors of the form $\begin{bmatrix}
      {2t} \\
      0 \\
      {- t}
      \end{bmatrix}.$ Show that $H$ is a subspace of $\text{ℝ}^{3}$. (Use the method of Exercise 9.)

Let $W$ be the set of all vectors of the form $\begin{bmatrix}
      {s + 3t} \\
      {s - t} \\
      {2s - t} \\
      {4t}
      \end{bmatrix}\,.$ Show that $W$ is a subspace of $\text{ℝ}^{4}$. (Use the method of Exercise 11.)

statement.math:
$$\begin{matrix}
      {c0 + ( - c0)} & = & {\lbrack c0 + c0\rbrack{+ ( - c0)}} & & & \\
      {c0 + ( - c0)} & = & {c0 + \left\lbrack c0 + ( - c0) \right\rbrack} & & & {\text{by~Axiom}\operatorname{\_\_\_\_\_}\left( \text{c} \right)} \\
      0 & = & {c0 + 0} & & & {\text{by~Axiom}\operatorname{\_\_\_\_\_}\left( \text{d} \right)} \\
      0 & = & {c0} & & & {\text{by~Axiom}\operatorname{\_\_\_\_\_}\left( \text{e} \right)}
      \end{matrix}$$
